/// How many times one run may be handed a loop-guard recovery note before the guard's
/// next verdict stops it.
///
/// One. A run that is going round, told what it is doing and what to do instead, and
/// does the same thing again has been given the answer already; a second note teaches
/// it only that the note can be ignored. Nothing resets this counter -- unlike the
/// tracker's own counts, which keep climbing through the recovery, so an identical
/// call straight after it reaches the next threshold and the run stops there.
const MAX_LOOP_RECOVERIES: u8 = 1;
