The flag's doc talks only about re-asking a looping completion (repetition detector), not the tool-loop guard. Since the flag now also gates this recovery, updating this doc comment is warranted (it's the CLI's user-facing help). This is a small, coherent addition. Let me add a paragraph:

```
    /// It also lets the tool-loop guard offer the run one recovery note before it
    /// stops a run that is repeating the same tool call: the note says what is being
    /// repeated and what to do instead, the run continues once, and a run that repeats
    /// again is stopped as it would have been.
```

Keep it concise and truthful (one note per run across rules).

Also the `RunSettings.loop_retries` doc in mod.rs describes only repetition re-ask. Update similarly. The issue says instructions third-party callers give extend naturally — but our own docs shouldn't be wrong. Add one paragraph to each.

Let me edit cli.rs.

